enes indicate bran  stark knew what would happen in the end  now we're back inside the three odd  ravens cave we hear leaf explain  why they created the night king  we were being slaughtered our sacred  trees cut down  we needed to defend ourselves from whom  from you in this final flashback scene  we see the night king when he laid his  finger on the face of one of craster's  sons  we're about to finally see what happens  after this  when the baby's eyes became blue the  night king gets back on his horse  while holding the baby we see him as  well as all the other white walkers ride  back to their castle in the lands of  always winter  we follow them as they walk inside the  castle then down a flight of stairs  they enter what looks like a crypt  similar to winterfell's the only  difference is  everything in this castle is either made  out of ice or carved into it  the night king bends down to set the  baby on a large block of ice  right as the night king stands back up  we get a better view of just how big  this crypt actually is  what it really looks like is an  underground mine shaft that stretches  out like very long fingers  into many different directions it makes  one wonder where they all lead  because you can only see so far into the  dark but this isn't the most shocking  reveal  right over the night king's shoulder we  can see there are dozens of babies  laying on blocks of ice  the blocks are in single file lines  stretching down each one of the shafts  until they disappear into the darkness  the flashbacks end when we cut to bran  stark sitting in the chair  his eyes are still rolled back in his  head but there's something different  about them  they're not as white as they used to be  they have somewhat of a blue haze to  them  after a few moments they flip back to  normal then we immediately  cut to the opening theme  like i said before all of these  flashback scenes will happen in the very  first episode before the opening credits  all of them foresh